# Defect 462's map, 2026-10-07. Symptom: a map read after its last release
# went on reading the freed block: a map made for four entries, released,
# then asked its length, answered at exit 0 (measured on this Mac at
# `56def9b4`). Cause: the key descriptor, which the runtime sets to none
# before a map's block goes (defect 314), was asked by a new reference and a
# release and never by a read. Now every reader asks it
# (`hero_map_require`, `runtime/parts/map.c`), and the read is named.
#
# The map is the C's own, made through the runtime and read after its
# release by a function of the program's own header: a map does not cross
# to C, and the compiler never reads one it has released. AddressSanitizer
# names the read of the freed block.

extern "fixedbugs-462-a-map-read-after-its-last-release-stops-at-the-read.h"
    function read_after_release(entries: i64) -> i64

function main()
    print("four entries, given back")
    print(read_after_release(entries: 4))
